    {
      "title": "Tata Trusts meet: SDTT approves over ₹150 crore in grants for 5 initiatives",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/companies/news/tata-trusts-meet-sdtt-approves-over-150-crore-in-grants-for-5-initiatives-126112000739_1.html",
      "description": "The Sir Dorabji Tata Trust approved over Rs 150 crore in grants to five initiatives, including Rs 50 crore to a hospital in Pune led by Jehangir H C Jehangir, who has been associated with other Tata Trusts.\nAll the proposals at the meeting chaired by Tata Trusts chairman Noel Tata, and also attended by Venu Srinivasan and Vijay Singh, people aware of the matter said.\nThere was no discussion at the meeting on any of the other issues within the Tata group dominating the headlines, they said.\nAmid questions raised over a grant being made to an entity with whom Jehangir, a trustee of the Sir Ratan Tata Trusts, is associated, a source asserted that there is \"no conflict of interest\" in this case.\nPune's Jehangir Hospital, which is promoted by the Cowasji Jehangir Trust counts on Jehangir HC Jehangir as the chief executive.\nSenior management of the hospital made a detailed presentation at the SDTT meeting held at the Tata Trusts office in Mumbai on Thursday, where they spoke about a Rs",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-20T11:01:43"
    }
